410, "total_tokens": 1410}}, "input": {"input": ["SANTANDER BANK:Santander Bank, formerly known as Bank Zachodni WBK, is one of the largest banks in Poland. It is renowned for its substantial client base and leadership in mobile banking services. As a major financial institution in the country, Santander Bank has established a strong presence in the banking sector, offering a wide range of services to meet the diverse needs of its customers. The bank's commitment to innovation and customer service has positioned it as a leader in the industry, particularly in the realm of digital and mobile banking solutions.", "ZBP:ZBP, or Związek Banków Polskich, is an association of Polish banks that publishes the Netb@nk reports", "MOBILE BANKING MARKET IN POLAND:The analysis of the mobile banking market in Poland centers on the use and development of mobile applications and cashless payment systems over the period from 2017 to 2021. This market study involves the creation of specific indicators designed to measure and compare the utilization of mobile applications against other forms of cashless payment systems. By focusing on these aspects, the analysis provides insights into the trends and shifts in consumer behavior regarding mobile banking and cashless transactions within Poland during this timeframe. The study aims to offer a comprehensive understanding of how mobile banking applications are being adopted and how they stack up against other cashless payment methods, reflecting the evolving landscape of financial technology in Poland.", "NETB@NK:Netb@nk is a report published by ZBP that provides data on the banking sector in Poland", "E-COMMERCE:E-commerce refers to online commercial transactions, which include pay-by-link transactions", "CASHLESS PAYMENT SYSTEMS:Cashless payment systems encompass a variety of methods for conducting transactions without the use of physical cash. These systems utilize digital means to facilitate payments, offering a convenient and efficient alternative to traditional cash transactions. Key components of cashless payment systems include the use of cards, such as credit and debit cards, which allow users to make purchases by swiping or tapping at point-of-sale terminals. Additionally, mobile apps play a significant role in cashless transactions, enabling users to pay for goods and services directly from their smartphones.\n\nAnother integral aspect of cashless payment systems is mobile payments, which have gained popularity due to their ease of use and accessibility. Mobile payment platforms allow users to link their bank accounts or credit cards to their mobile devices, enabling seamless transactions with just a few taps. This method is particularly advantageous for on-the-go purchases and is widely accepted by retailers and service providers.\n\nOnline banking is also a crucial component of cashless payment systems, providing users with the ability to conduct financial transactions over the internet. This includes transferring funds, paying bills, and making purchases from online retailers. Online banking offers the convenience of managing finances from anywhere with an internet connection, further reducing the need for physical cash.\n\nOverall, cashless payment systems offer a modern and efficient way to handle financial transactions, reducing the reliance on cash and enhancing the speed and security of payments. As technology continues to advance, these systems are expected to become even more integrated into daily life, offering users greater flexibility and control over their financial activities.", "BANKING APPLICATIONS:", "PAYMENT CARDS:Payment cards are physical or virtual cards used to make transactions, including credit, debit, and prepaid cards", "VIRTUAL DIGITAL WALLETS:Virtual digital wallets are online services or apps that store payment information and allow users to make electronic transactions", "HCE CARDS:HCE CARDS, or Host Card Emulation cards, are virtual cards utilized in digital wallets to facilitate contactless payments. These cards have experienced notable growth, particularly in Poland, where their adoption has been significant. From 2017 to 2019, HCE cards saw a marked increase in usage, reflecting a broader trend towards the adoption of smartphone-based payment solutions. This trend continued beyond 2019, with the usage of HCE cards rising from 2% in 2017 to 16.1% by 2021. This increase highlights the growing consumer preference for digital and contactless payment methods, driven by the convenience and security offered by smartphone technology. As a result, HCE cards have become an integral part of the evolving landscape of digital payments, contributing to the shift away from traditional physical cards towards more modern, virtual solutions.", "DIGITAL WALLETS:", "COVID-19 PANDEMIC:The COVID-19 pandemic, a global health crisis that began in 2020, had profound and far-reaching impacts on various aspects of life worldwide, including in Poland. It led to the declaration of a state of epidemic in Poland, prompting significant administrative changes across multiple sectors. One of the most notable effects of the pandemic was its influence on consumer behavior and payment trends. As physical trade faced restrictions, there was a marked increase in online transactions and e-commerce activities. This shift was accompanied by a growing preference for cashless transactions, as consumers and businesses alike sought safer and more convenient payment methods.\n\nIn Poland, the pandemic accelerated the adoption of digital payment systems, such as BLIK, and increased the popularity of online shopping. The demand for payment cards surged as consumers adapted to new shopping habits. Additionally, the pandemic spurred a significant rise in mobile banking usage, particularly among older generations who had previously been less inclined to use digital financial services. This shift was partly driven by the necessity to minimize physical contact and adhere to social distancing measures.\n\nThe retail and service sectors in Poland also underwent administrative changes, with a strong emphasis on promoting cashless payments to reduce the risk of virus transmission. These changes were part of broader efforts to adapt to the new normal and ensure the safety of both consumers and employees.\n\nOverall, the COVID-19 pandemic acted as a catalyst for digital transformation in Poland's financial landscape, influencing consumer behavior and accelerating the adoption of cashless and online payment systems. The increased use of mobile banking and payment platforms like BLIK among all age groups, including the oldest consumers, highlights the pandemic's role in reshaping financial habits and preferences.", "TRADITIONAL PAYMENT CARDS:Traditional payment cards were the most popular form of payment during the pandemic, although their demand was affected by the rise of online shopping and the introduction of contactless systems like BLIK", "POS:Point of Sale (POS) systems are essential tools used for processing card transactions in physical retail environments. In Poland, these systems have demonstrated a steady increase in usage from 2017 to 2021. This growth trend was notably influenced by the COVID-19 pandemic, during which there was a significant rise in card transactions. The pandemic accelerated the adoption of cashless payment methods, as consumers and businesses alike sought safer and more convenient transaction options. As a result, POS systems have become increasingly integral to the retail experience, facilitating efficient and secure payment processing.", "MOBILE ONLY:The trend of users relying solely on mobile banking applications for their banking needs, which increased from 40.8% in 2017 to 61.6% in 2021 in Poland", "PAY-BY-LINK:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_8c26e1b4c10f0b9c4b8499bd93e428f61e59b5451d2e491e9d7d574148b0ca38_v2"}